{"id": "EUVD-2026-95425", "enisaUuid": "f1917ecf-dc23-35eb-9a98-f1ca2d556c34", "description": "Historically, we have been rather lax about malformed framing-related headers in our HTTP/2 implementation, as they cannot interfere with HTTP/2 framing. However, this makes it possible for our HTTP/2 implementation to forward responses containing such headers to an HTTP/1 client when acting as a reverse proxy. If the HTTP/1 client also does not behave strictly enough, this can result in response smuggling.", "datePublished": "2026-10-08T22:53:59", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-09T16:23:56", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:N", "references": ["https://go.dev/cl/835145", "https://go.dev/cl/836385", "https://go.dev/issue/81115", "https://groups.google.com/g/golang-announce/c/U2fTuyDJznI", "https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2026-6610"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-78660"], "assigner": "Go", "epss": 0.3, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "03754fba-1e7b-391a-884b-c116ca0753e8", "product": {"name": "net/http/internal/http2", "vendor": {"name": "Go standard library"}}, "product_version": "1.27.0-0 <1.27.2"}, {"id": "28d92cd8-42ae-3753-9464-0e3a21b5838c", "product": {"name": "golang.org/x/net/http2", "vendor": {"name": "golang.org/x/net"}}, "product_version": "0 <0.60.0"}, {"id": "a9ce1404-3050-313f-bad9-2bec9471c448", "product": {"name": "net/http", "vendor": {"name": "Go standard library"}}, "product_version": "0 <1.26.9"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "81768263-badb-3f0e-861d-e3c237933e0b", "vendor": {"name": "golang.org/x/net"}}, {"id": "8787fe26-0d36-3310-b9b6-51480e399e9a", "vendor": {"name": "Go standard library"}}], "isExploited": false}